theory.intro:
To estimate the area under $y=f(x)$ from $x=a$ to $x=b$, cut the interval into $n$ strips of width $h=\frac{b-a}{n}$. Build a rectangle on each strip and add their areas. Taking each height at the strip's left edge, right edge or midpoint gives three different estimates.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) rectangle (2,0.75);
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) rectangle (3,1.5);
\fill[gray!35] (3,0) rectangle (4,2.75);
\draw (1,0) rectangle (2,0.75);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (3,1.5);
\draw (3,0) rectangle (4,2.75);
\draw[->] (-0.3,0) -- (5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.3) -- (0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,->,domain=0:4.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.25*\x*\x+0.5});
\node[below] at (1,-0.1) {$a$};
\node[below] at (4,-0.1) {$b$};
\node at (1.7,4.5) {left endpoints};
\begin{scope}[xshift=6cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) rectangle (2,1.5);
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) rectangle (3,2.75);
\fill[gray!35] (3,0) rectangle (4,4.5);
\draw (1,0) rectangle (2,1.5);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (3,2.75);
\draw (3,0) rectangle (4,4.5);
\draw[->] (-0.3,0) -- (5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.3) -- (0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,->,domain=0:4.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.25*\x*\x+0.5});
\node[below] at (1,-0.1) {$a$};
\node[below] at (4,-0.1) {$b$};
\node at (1.7,5) {right endpoints};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

