mastery.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=0.4cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) rectangle (1.5,1);
\fill[gray!35] (1.5,0) rectangle (2,2.25);
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) rectangle (2.5,4);
\fill[gray!35] (2.5,0) rectangle (3,6.25);
\draw (1,0) rectangle (1.5,1);
\draw (1.5,0) rectangle (2,2.25);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (2.5,4);
\draw (2.5,0) rectangle (3,6.25);
\draw[->] (-0.3,0) -- (3.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.4) -- (0,12.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,->,domain=0:3.3,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x});
\node at (1.1,11) {left endpoints};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3} \draw (\x,0.4) -- (\x,-0.4) node[below] {$\x$};
\begin{scope}[xshift=5.2cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) rectangle (1.5,2.25);
\fill[gray!35] (1.5,0) rectangle (2,4);
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) rectangle (2.5,6.25);
\fill[gray!35] (2.5,0) rectangle (3,9);
\draw (1,0) rectangle (1.5,2.25);
\draw (1.5,0) rectangle (2,4);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (2.5,6.25);
\draw (2.5,0) rectangle (3,9);
\draw[->] (-0.3,0) -- (3.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.4) -- (0,12.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,->,domain=0:3.3,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x});
\node at (1.15,11.6) {right endpoints};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3} \draw (\x,0.4) -- (\x,-0.4) node[below] {$\x$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The area under $y=x^{2}$ from $x=1$ to $x=3$ is estimated with $4$ strips, using left endpoints and then right endpoints.
Find both estimates, and state what they tell you about the true area.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=0.22cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) rectangle (1,19.75);
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) rectangle (2,17.75);
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) rectangle (3,13.75);
\fill[gray!35] (3,0) rectangle (4,7.75);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (1,19.75);
\draw (1,0) rectangle (2,17.75);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (3,13.75);
\draw (3,0) rectangle (4,7.75);
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.6) -- (0,23.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,->,domain=0:4.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{20-\x*\x});
\fill (0.5,19.75) circle (2pt);
\fill (1.5,17.75) circle (2pt);
\fill (2.5,13.75) circle (2pt);
\fill (3.5,7.75) circle (2pt);
\node at (2.6,22) {$y=20-x^{2}$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} \draw (\x,0.8) -- (\x,-0.8) node[below] {$\x$};
