\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The $4$ rectangles shown use the midpoint of each strip.
Find the midpoint estimate for the area under $y=20-x^{2}$ from $x=0$ to $x=4$, then find the right-endpoint estimate for the same $4$ strips, and say which of the two must be smaller than the true area.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=0.25cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) rectangle (1,2);
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) rectangle (2,3);
