\draw (1,0) rectangle (2,3);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (3,6);
\draw (3,0) rectangle (4,11);
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (5,0) node[right] {$t$ (min)};
\draw[->] (0,-2.4) -- (0,23.4) node[above] {$R$ (L/min)};
\draw[thick,->,domain=0:4.3,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2+\x*\x});
\node at (1.2,17) {$R=2+t^{2}$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} \draw (\x,0.7) -- (\x,-0.7) node[below] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {5,10,15,20} \draw (0.05,\y) -- (-0.05,\y) node[left] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Water flows into a tank at a rate $R=2+t^{2}$ litres per minute, for $0\le t\le 4$ minutes.
Use the $4$ left-endpoint rectangles shown to estimate the volume that flows in, and say whether the true volume is larger or smaller than your estimate.
